    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The average value is given by adding all the values and dividing by the number of values.\nThus,\n$$\n\\frac{0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z}{5} = \\frac{30z}{5} = \\boxed{6z}.\n$$\n\nExplanation:\n\n**\n\n1. Identify the individual values: 0, 2z, 4z, 8z, and 16z.\n2. Calculate the sum of these values:\n   \\[\n   0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z = 30z\n   \\]\n3. Determine the number of values, which is 5 (since there are five numbers in the list).\n4. Compute the average by dividing the sum by the number of values:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{30z}{5} = 6z\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the average value is $\\boxed{6z}$.\n\n**Proof:**\n\n1. Apply the formula for the average of a set of numbers:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of numbers}}{\\text{Number of values}}\n   \\]\n2. Substitute the values and the number of values:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z}{5}\n   \\]\n3. Simplify the numerator (sum of the values):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{30z}{5}\n   \\]\n4. The average is 6z, as shown in the solution.",
